From 2f6ce655d0c9d6905752001df6049d6766aa47d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frederic Petrignani <frederic.petrignani@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:29:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cc: RCCSD(T) lambda and response-density (T) intermediates in
 C

The (T) parts of ccsd_t_lambda.make_intermediates and of
ccsd_t_rdm._gamma1_intermediates / _gamma2_intermediates are computed per
virtual triple in lib/cc/ccsd_t_rdm.c (CCsd_t_lambda_intermediates,
CCsd_t_rdm_intermediates) with thread-private nocc^3 buffers, on the pattern
of the (T) energy kernel, instead of blocked lib.einsum over six-index
blocks. Signatures and finishing steps of the Python functions unchanged.
Benzene/cc-pVDZ, 16 threads: make_intermediates 397 -> 24 s, RCCSD(T)
gradient with given lambda 1004 -> 70 s; results equal to 1e-16 on
identical amplitudes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
